      "summary": "Cardrona Alpine Resort is open for skiing today, a beautiful spring day with bluebird skies and moderate southwesterly winds. It'll start out cool and warm up quickly with the sun; snow conditions and coverage are described as superb, with fresh snow and cold temps giving good grooming up high. There's been 27 cm over the past 7 days, holding the natural base at 112 cm; it's currently 3°C with winds around 13 km/h gusting to 21 km/h. The lower mountain starts firm, with off-piste variable to start before softening nicely as the day warms. All 10 of 10 lifts are open. Main Basin and Valley View are running from 8:30am, with the T-Bar, Captains, Soho and Willow following; the Olympic Halfpipe and Platter had a delayed start to allow salting, now fully open from 10am. 7 of 9 park features are open, with all 10 of 10 terrain zones open. The Junior Nationals are running Slopestyle today in Lil Bucks and Antlers Alley, briefing from 8:30am. The access road is chain-free, with an active road hazard advisory in place. The spring Pines Shuttle and bus schedule begins tomorrow, 1 October (up: 8:30/9:30/10:30am; down: 1:30/2:30/3:30/4:15pm). Upper car parks are nearly at capacity today. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 10 / 10 Runs Open - / 38 Percent open 100 %",
